'A quantity phrase combines a number with a classifier, usually followed by the noun: 三个鸡蛋, 两杯水. When the object is already understood, the noun can be omitted: 我要两个. 半 precedes the classifier. Some amounts name a portion rather than an object: 半杯奶 is a measured amount of milk.',[
('我买六个鸡蛋，你要几个？','I am buying six eggs. How many would you like?'),('我要两个，还要半杯奶。','I would like two, and half a cup of milk.')],
